  <section id="understanding-la-time" class="reveal" aria-label="Understanding Los Angeles Time">
    <h2>1. Understanding Los Angeles Time</h2>
    <p>
      Located on the west coast of North America, Los Angeles is the second-most populous city in the United States and the cultural capital of the Western region. Its local time dictates the tempo of major global industries, particularly modern entertainment, digital tech startups, aerospace engineering, and international shipping.
    </p>
    <p>
      The term <strong>Pacific Time (PT)</strong> is a general designation representing the active offset inside the Pacific Time Zone. It adapts to seasonal changes, using two distinct offsets:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Pacific Standard Time (PST):</strong> Used during the autumn and winter months. It is 8 hours behind Coordinated Universal Time (UTC-8).</li>
      <li><strong>Pacific Daylight Time (PDT):</strong> Used during the spring and summer months. It is 7 hours behind Coordinated Universal Time (UTC-7).</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- Did You Know Box -->
    <div class="did-you-know">
      <h4>Did You Know?</h4>
      <p>
        The entire state of California operates under Pacific Time. The boundary lines for Pacific Time extend north through Oregon and Washington, east to the borders of Idaho and Nevada, and south to the Mexican border.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Visual 2: California Time Zone Map -->
