  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 5: WHY LOS ANGELES USES PACIFIC TIME
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="why-la-uses-pacific-time" class="reveal" aria-label="Why Los Angeles Uses Pacific Time">
    <h2>3. Why Los Angeles Uses Pacific Time</h2>
    <p>
      The establishment of standard time zones was not an overnight decision. Prior to the late 19th century, cities across North America calculated local time by observing noon (when the sun reached its highest point). This created hundreds of localized offsets, rendering railroad coordination almost impossible and leading to numerous accidents.
    </p>
    <p>
      In 1883, the major railroad companies of North America collaborated to split the continent into four primary time zones: Eastern, Central, Mountain, and Pacific. Los Angeles was placed in the Pacific zone due to its longitude, which sits close to the 120th meridian west of Greenwich. The International Meridian Conference of 1884 solidified these zones globally, anchoring them to the prime meridian at Greenwich, London.
    </p>
    <p>
      Today, California maintains this alignment under the oversight of the <strong>U.S. Department of Transportation</strong>, which regulates standard time and DST transition rules to facilitate national commerce, air travel, and interstate shipping.
    </p>

    <!-- Expert Tip -->
    <div class="tip-box">
      <h3>Expert Tip: Permanent DST Debates</h3>
      <p>
        While voters in California approved Proposition 7 in 2018 (which cleared the path to establish permanent Daylight Saving Time), any permanent change requires a change in federal law. The federal Sunshine Protection Act has been proposed but not enacted, meaning the biannual clock changes remain active.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 6: LOS ANGELES BUSINESS HOURS
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="la-business-hours" class="reveal" aria-label="Los Angeles Business Hours">
    <h2>4. Los Angeles Business &amp; Industry Scheduling</h2>
    <p>
      As a major global commercial hub, Los Angeles houses specific business cultures with strict scheduling cycles. Navigating these cycles is vital for partnerships, communications, and logistical planning.
    </p>

    <h3>Hollywood &amp; The Entertainment Industry</h3>
    <p>
      Hollywood operates on a fast-paced scheduling model governed by "call times." Call sheets are distributed in Pacific Time (PT), indicating when actors, technicians, and crew members must report to set. These call times are determined based on local sunrise and sunset to ensure optimal natural light for filming.
    </p>
    <p>
      For international co-productions (e.g., coordinating between a soundstage in London and a post-production house in Santa Monica), directors and coordinators must convert times between BST/GMT and PDT/PST to avoid crew downtime and scheduling clashes.
    </p>

    <!-- Visual 5: Hollywood Production Schedule -->
    <figure class="article-image-container">
