    <h3>Jet Lag Adjustment Strategies</h3>
    <p>
      When flying into Los Angeles from the East Coast or international cities, your internal circadian rhythm will be desynchronized from local solar cycles. Use these expert strategies to adapt quickly:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Pre-adjust your schedule:</strong> Shift your bedtime by 1–2 hours toward Pacific Time several days before departure.</li>
      <li><strong>Control light exposure:</strong> Seek bright California sunlight in the morning if you are arriving from Asia, or in the late afternoon if you are arriving from Europe.</li>
      <li><strong>Stay hydrated:</strong> Air cabin pressure accelerates dehydration, which worsens the physical symptoms of jet lag.</li>
      <li><strong>Align meals:</strong> Force yourself to eat meals according to local Los Angeles time upon landing, helping reset your peripheral body clocks.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

