    <h2>8. Common Time Zone Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
    <p>
      Coordinating with Los Angeles requires close attention to detail. Avoid these frequent errors:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Confusing PST with PDT:</strong> Using PST during the summer (when Los Angeles is on PDT) indicates a UTC-8 offset, which is incorrect by one hour. Refer to local time as Pacific Time (PT) if you are unsure.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Assuming Arizona Shares California's Time Zone:</strong> Arizona operates on Mountain Standard Time (MST, UTC-7) year-round and does not observe DST. While Arizona and California share the same clock time in summer, Arizona is one hour ahead in winter.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Forgetting the Transition Gaps:</strong> Europe and North America switch to and from DST on different dates. The time gap between London and Los Angeles changes from 8 hours to 7 hours for a few weeks in March and October.
      </li>
    </ol>

